      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "1",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 1:1"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "1",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.1.1",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.1.1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "2",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 1:2"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "2",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "King Ahaziah of Israel fell off the balcony on the roof of his palace in Samaria and was seriously injured. So he sent some messengers to consult Baalzebub, the god of the Philistine city of Ekron, in order to find out whether or not he would recover. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.1.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.1.2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "3",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 1:3"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "3",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But an angel of the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.1.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.1.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " commanded Elijah, the prophet from Tishbe, to go and meet the messengers of King Ahaziah and ask them, “Why are you going to consult Baalzebub, the god of Ekron? Is it because you think there is no god in Israel? ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.1.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.1.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "4",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 1:4"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Tell the king that the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.1.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.1.4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " says, ‘You will not recover from your injuries; you will die!’ ”",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.1.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.1.4"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
